  "method": "Total variance is pair-sampling plus label noise. The pair-sampling standard deviation is recovered separately for each arm of the committed percentile bootstrap interval, because that interval is not symmetric about the point estimate and treating it as symmetric moves the lower bound away from zero. Label noise is modelled as an independent flip with probability p per label, so the flip count on each class is binomial and its variance is n*p*(1-p); that count is carried into MCC by the per-flip sensitivity of the observed confusion matrix. The point estimate is held fixed, so this bounds the interval and is not a posterior.",
  "worst_case": "p = 0.5 makes every label an independent fair coin, which is the largest label noise any model can assert."
 }
